From: Loïc Vigneron <loic@spin42.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: monaco-monza-som: Give the Ethernet SerDes its supplies

The SGMII SerDes driver takes a 0.9 V supply (vdda-0p9) and a 1.2 V
supply (vdda-1p2); the deprecated phy-supply it is given here is not
used, so the PHY runs on dummy regulators. The 0.9 V rail, L4A, is then
held only by the display and camera PHYs: with no HDMI display, or once
it is unplugged, nothing holds L4A, the kernel turns it off, the SerDes
PLL no longer locks and Ethernet stops. Give the SerDes L4A and L5A.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-monza-som.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-monza-som.dtsi
@@ -284,7 +284,8 @@
 
 /* Ethernet/SGMII */
 &serdes0 {
-	phy-supply = <&vreg_l5a>;
+	vdda-0p9-supply = <&vreg_l4a>;
+	vdda-1p2-supply = <&vreg_l5a>;
 
 	status = "okay";
 };
